#: 3a298c3db1bb4206b9ff9a0eae16e9d6
#: 93643f4296fc4ba7a0bba71ba237e2ff
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_BAUD <SERIAL4_BAUD>` = 115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:42
#: 3a7e7306da3a4d07a59bdda752d26e70
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` =  5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:45
#: cae43a937eef47a09b040df7eda95260
msgid "ELRS Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:47
#: cc9f98c4341c4eae9e1fec1d4510a1c6
msgid "ELRS can be setup in the same manner as CRSF above , however, bit 13 of :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` should be set to alter the baudrate from 416KBaud that CRSF uses, to 420KBaud that ELRS uses when in CRSF compatible protocol mode. As mentioned above, the UART selected must have DMA capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:49
#: 8146b6709ce5468f824e8380ff7d33cd
msgid "ELRS can also be configured to output MAVLink, enabling full bidirectional Mavlink telemetry and RC control over the same link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:52
#: bcbab1329dce4c929eaa9702c8fe793e
msgid "ELRS MAVLink Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:54
#: 45e61d3886de4a1a9578b253bbbe2192
msgid "Instead of CRSF protocol, MAVLink protocol can be used if the receiver is configured for it. In this case, using SERIAL 4 for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:58
#: 57d790736cd54f53a974446860f56fe1
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` = 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:60
#: e8dc5e86a8e84c74821fe05b8bacdd58
msgid "If the ELRS transmitter module has WIFI capability, then the telemetry data can be forwarded wirelessly to a PC or phone based GCS close to the transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:63
#: 809bc4385bd343efbc62e4b556142b5a
msgid "ELRS bootloader \"lockup\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:65
#: ee079dd1ef6348d9aa434079baf790bd
msgid "Some ELRS receivers can appear to be locked up in \"bootloader\" mode when the autopilot system is powered on. This is usually due to the UART RX pin to which they are attached being held low during power application, which ELRS interprets as being forced into bootloader mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:67
#: 285b6e2ad8b4403a9cf94c64a10078e9
msgid "The most common cause for this is when the autopilot board also has a DJI HD VTX attached and the SBUS pin of that interface is directly tied to the UART RX pin being used for RC input from the ELRS. If the VTX is not powered up at the same time as the ELRS, the SBUS output will act as a current sink for the ELRS TX pin and force it into bootloader. This occurs if the autopilot is only being powered from USB or the autopilot bootloader forces the HD VTX power supply off on boot(so that the pilot must toggle a transmitter switch to actively turn it on, for power/heat saving). The simple solution is to remove the SBUS wire going from the HD VTX to the DJI connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:70
#: 803819b1ad624177aacb0dc2de752d2a
msgid "CRSF Video Transmitters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:72
#: 7e7d6555d526478c84773f43054ab2cf
msgid "TBS Video Transmitters can also be connected to ArduPilot using the CRSF protocol. This allows the VTX to be configured via parameters and, for VTXs such as the `TBS Unify Evo <https://www.team-blacksheep.com/products/prod:tbs_unify_evo>`__ , receive telemetry data that can be displayed using the built-in OSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:74
#: d52d2b1a47a1493c9ec4a091778cda37
msgid "If you are using CRSF for RC input as well then nothing more needs to be done in order to enable VTX control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:76
#: 7f19a92b5c0d4b548768ef16cb3077be
msgid "If you only wish to use CRSF for VTX control then connect the VTX to the UART in the normal way - TX to RX and RX to TX and configure the UART connection as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:78
#: 905756c17a8140fd92939ca3c316ccb4
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 29"
msgstr ""
